Run:  python3 book_demo.py              (prints the whole book)
      python3 book_demo.py 3            (prints chapter 3 only)
      python3 book_demo.py search WORD  (finds WORD across chapters)
      python3 book_demo.py html         (writes book.html)
"""
import json, sys, html as _h

BOOK = {'title': 'The Last Spell', 'author': 'Signature original', 'genre': 'Epic Quests', 'chapters': [{'n': 1, 'title': 'The Call', 'text': 'Finnian Vale slept that night with the rune glowing faintly, and dreamed of the Sunken City of Mar in flames. They woke with the taste of smoke and a single thought: courage lights the dark.\n\nAt the first standing stone, Finnian Vale found the mark — the ancient rune of the bearers of the Scroll of Binding. It warmed under their hand. The quest, it seemed, had been waiting.\n\nFinnian Vale was mending a fence in the Sunken City of Mar when the sky went dark at noon. The elders whispered: the necromancer Sylas had taken the Scroll of Binding, and the old magic was failing. Prophecy or not, someone had to go.'}, {'n': 2, 'title': 'Trials of the Road', 'text': "They were ambushed by the necromancer Sylas's riders at the enchanted glade. Finnian Vale fought with a mithril blade borrowed from the elf Luthien Silverleaf, and learned that bravery is mostly refusing to run at the right moment.\n\nAt the moonwell they met a seer who spoke of the Scroll of Binding: 'It is not a weapon,' she said, 'though it can kill. It is not a shield, though it can save. It is a promise — and promises are the heaviest magic.'\n\nOn the seventh night, Finnian Vale found the Scroll of Binding's trail — a shimmer in the air, a song half-heard. It was close now. And the necromancer Sylas knew they were coming."}, {'n': 3, 'title': 'The Descent', 'text': "Alarms rang. the necromancer Sylas's army closed in. the elf Luthien Silverleaf barred the door with a fallen pillar and grinned. 'Go,' they said. 'I'll hold them.' Finnian Vale refused to leave — so they held it together, back to back, as the dark came on.\n\nThey found the Scroll of Binding in the vault of whispers, guarded by the dragon Karthax. The beast spoke: 'Take it, little bearer, if you can answer: what is stronger than dragonfire?' Finnian Vale answered: 'courage lights the dark.' The dragon bowed and let them pass.\n\nThe dungeons held prisoners from every corner of the Sunken City of Mar, and Finnian Vale freed them all, though it slowed the quest. 'the Scroll of Binding can wait an hour,' Finnian Vale said. 'People cannot.' the elf Luthien Silverleaf never loved them more."}, {'n': 4, 'title': 'The Price', 'text': "They escaped the fortress by griffon, the Scroll of Binding burning like a small sun. But the elf Luthien Silverleaf was wounded, and the wound festered with dark magic. The healers said only the Scroll of Binding itself could cure it — at the cost of its power.\n\nThey marched on the necromancer Sylas's stronghold with the Scroll of Binding dark but their hearts lit. Finnian Vale carried it anyway, empty as it was. Symbols, the elf Luthien Silverleaf said, have their own magic.\n\nthe elf Luthien Silverleaf woke and wept to see it. 'The prophecy—' they began. Finnian Vale said: 'Prophecies are poems, not orders.' But the army of the necromancer Sylas was coming, and they had no magic left."}, {'n': 5, 'title': 'The Breaking of the Dark', 'text': "Then Finnian Vale remembered the seer's words and the dragon's riddle, and did the last thing the necromancer Sylas expected: Finnian Vale offered mercy. 'Yield,' Finnian Vale said, 'and live.' the necromancer Sylas laughed — and in that laugh, the dark wavered.\n\nthe Scroll of Binding, dark and cold so long, blazed sudden white — fed not by magic but by the choice. The light struck the necromancer Sylas's armor and the armor was empty; the dark lord was only a frightened soul inside, and the soul, seen, fled.\n\nThe battle for the Sunken City of Mar raged from dawn to dusk. the necromancer Sylas rode out in black armor, terrible and splendid, and challenged Finnian Vale single combat. The armies held their breath."}, {'n': 6, 'title': 'The Return', 'text': "the elf Luthien Silverleaf was given the highest honor of the Sunken City of Mar and immediately used it to demand better roads. Finnian Vale was offered a throne and laughed until they cried. 'I mend fences,' Finnian Vale said.\n\nthe Scroll of Binding was set in the great hall, where children touch it for luck. It never blazed again — but on dark nights, travelers swear it glows faintly, like a coal that remembers fire.\n\nAnd the choice, the songs say, is always the same: courage lights the dark. In the Sunken City of Mar and everywhere, forever."}]}

def word_count():
    return sum(len(c["text"].split()) for c in BOOK["chapters"])

def print_book(ch=None):
    print("=" * 64)
    print(BOOK["title"].upper(), "\nby", BOOK["author"], "-", BOOK["genre"])
    print("=" * 64)
    for c in BOOK["chapters"]:
        if ch and c["n"] != ch:
            continue
        print("\n\nCHAPTER %d: %s\n%s" % (c["n"], c["title"], "-" * 40))
        print(c["text"])
    print("\n[%d words, %d chapters — complete]" % (word_count(), len(BOOK["chapters"])))

def search(word):
    w = word.lower()
    for c in BOOK["chapters"]:
        for i, para in enumerate(c["text"].split("\n\n")):
            if w in para.lower():
                print("[ch %d, para %d] %s..." % (c["n"], i + 1, para[:160].replace("\n", " ")))

def write_html(path="book.html"):
    parts = ["<html><head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>%s</title></head><body>" % _h.escape(BOOK["title"])]
    parts.append("<h1>%s</h1><p><i>by %s — %s</i></p>" % (_h.escape(BOOK["title"]), _h.escape(BOOK["author"]), _h.escape(BOOK["genre"])))
    for c in BOOK["chapters"]:
        parts.append("<h2>Chapter %d: %s</h2>" % (c["n"], _h.escape(c["title"])))
        for para in c["text"].split("\n\n"):
            parts.append("<p>%s</p>" % _h.escape(para))
    parts.append("</body></html>")
    open(path, "w").write("\n".join(parts))
    print("wrote", path)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    a = sys.argv[1:]
    if a and a[0] == "html":
        write_html()
    elif len(a) >= 2 and a[0] == "search":
        search(a[1])
    elif a and a[0].isdigit():
        print_book(int(a[0]))
    else:
        print_book()

